# Package profile: one package per line, added on top of configs/ra81-nss.config.
#   name        build the package into the image
#   -name       leave a package that would otherwise be included out of the image
# Packages must come from a feed in upstream/feeds.conf. The build fails if a
# listed package does not end up in the image (unknown name, missing feed,
# unmet dependency), so an upgrade never drops software silently.
#
# The default profile adds no package. It does leave two out: this build uses
# the single-slot layout, and the firmware updater needs two.
#
# ra81-ota flashes "the slot that is not running" and arms a trial boot through
# /lib/functions/xiaomi-dualboot.sh + flag_* - none of which exist without a
# second slot. Built in, it would either fail on every install or write to a
# rootfs_1 partition that is not there. Upgrade with sysupgrade or the U-Boot
# web page instead (README, "Installing").
-ra81-ota
-luci-app-ra81-ota
